Wire standalone A-MSDU TX into the rtl8822cu USB xmit path (v2).

Realtek only ever wired the A-MSDU coalesce builder and the per-AC hold timers into
the PCIe xmit path (hal/*/pci/*ce_xmit.c). On USB they are dead code with no caller,
so the `tx_amsdu` proc knob is inert and the counters never move.

v1 of this patch spammed "RTW: xmit_status_check tx hang" and STAs stopped
associating. Two distinct bugs, both fixed here:

 (1) XMITBUF LEAK. v1's "could not pair" branch called rtw_dump_xframe() on a frame
     that had never been through rtw_xmitframe_coalesce(), so pattrib->nr_frags and
     ->last_txcmdsz were never set and no txdesc was built. rtw_dump_xframe() submits
     the URB *inside* `for (t = 0; t < pattrib->nr_frags; t++)`, so with nr_frags == 0
     nothing was written and the xmit_buf was never returned by the TX-complete
     callback: one leaked xmitbuf per event until the pool was exhausted.
     Measured on real HW: amsdu_debug_coalesce_one=4, coalesce_two=0, 137 tx-hang
     prints, wlan0 TX 0 kbps, majestic's UDP socket wedged with 64 KB in Send-Q.
     Fixed by routing every non-paired frame through one helper that does the FULL
     normal setup (buffer, agg_num, pkt_offset, coalesce, os_xmit_complete) before
     dumping. There is now exactly one hand-rolled single-frame path, not two.

 (2) MISSING pkt_offset / agg_num. rtw_xmitframe_coalesce_amsdu() computes
     hw_hdr_offset = TXDESC_SIZE + (pxmitframe->pkt_offset * PACKET_OFFSET_SZ) under
     CONFIG_USB_TX_AGGREGATION, and update_txdesc() uses pkt_offset to decide whether
     to pull the txdesc head. v1 left both zero, so even a successfully coalesced
     A-MSDU was built at the wrong offset for the USB bulk path.

Also added, and the reason v1 could never have helped even without the hang: the
realtek tx_amsdu==2 HOLD TIMER. At FPV rates the USB TX queue drains each frame
before a second one co-queues, so opportunistic pairing never fires (coalesce_two
stayed 0 = zero aggregation benefit). When exactly one A-MSDU-able frame is queued we
arm the per-AC 1 ms timer and return without sending; the timeout handler already
does tasklet_hi_schedule(xmit_tasklet), so a held frame is always re-driven and can
never stall. Added latency is bounded by 1 ms and only occurs when the queue would
otherwise be idle.

Correctness note: all subframes of one A-MSDU must share RA and TID.
rtw_dequeue_xframe() walks the per-AC hwxmit queues and can return frames for
different stations, so we verify RA + priority before pairing. The PCIe reference
omits this check; it is harmless with max_num_sta=1 but wrong in general.

diff --git a/hal/rtl8822c/usb/rtl8822cu_xmit.c b/hal/rtl8822c/usb/rtl8822cu_xmit.c
--- a/hal/rtl8822c/usb/rtl8822cu_xmit.c
+++ b/hal/rtl8822c/usb/rtl8822cu_xmit.c
@@ -496,6 +496,51 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_TX_AGGREGATION
 #define IDEA_CONDITION 1	/* check all packets before enqueue */
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_TX_AMSDU
+/* Send one already-dequeued frame the way the normal first-frame path would.
+ * Every field here matters on USB: agg_num must be 1, pkt_offset reserves the
+ * bulk-out block-check offset that update_txdesc() and rtw_xmitframe_coalesce_amsdu()
+ * read back, and rtw_xmitframe_coalesce() is what actually builds the 802.11 header +
+ * txdesc and sets nr_frags/last_txcmdsz. Skipping any of them makes rtw_dump_xframe()
+ * write nothing (its URB submit sits inside `for (t = 0; t < nr_frags; t++)`) and leak
+ * the xmit_buf -- that was the v1 TX hang. Consumes the frame either way. */
+static s32 rtl8822cu_amsdu_send_single(PADAPTER padapter,
+		struct xmit_priv *pxmitpriv, struct xmit_frame *pf)
+{
+	struct xmit_buf *sbuf;
+
+	if (pf == NULL)
+		return _FALSE;
+
+	sbuf = rtw_alloc_xmitbuf(pxmitpriv);
+	if (sbuf == NULL) {
+		rtw_free_xmitframe(pxmitpriv, pf);
+		return _FALSE;
+	}
+
+	pf->pxmitbuf = sbuf;
+	pf->buf_addr = sbuf->pbuf;
+	sbuf->priv_data = pf;
+	pf->agg_num = 1;
+#ifdef CONFIG_TX_EARLY_MODE
+	pf->pkt_offset = (PACKET_OFFSET_SZ / 8) + 1;
+#else
+	pf->pkt_offset = (PACKET_OFFSET_SZ / 8);
+#endif
+
+	if (rtw_xmitframe_coalesce(padapter, pf->pkt, pf) == _FALSE) {
+		rtw_free_xmitbuf(pxmitpriv, sbuf);
+		rtw_free_xmitframe(pxmitpriv, pf);
+		return _FALSE;
+	}
+
+	rtw_os_xmit_complete(padapter, pf);
+	rtw_dump_xframe(padapter, pf);
+	return _TRUE;
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_TX_AMSDU */
+
 static s32 rtl8822cu_xmitframe_complete(PADAPTER padapter, struct xmit_priv *pxmitpriv, struct xmit_buf *pxmitbuf)
 {
 	HAL_DATA_TYPE	*pHalData = GET_HAL_DATA(padapter);
